<title>FRANCE: Contest for seats narrows in IFOP French poll.</title>
<headline>Contest for seats narrows in IFOP French poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an opinion poll of voters' intentions ahead of the May 25/June 1 two-round parliamentary election.</p>
<p>The telephone poll of 1,003 registered voters was conducted by IFOP on May 16 for the Journal du Dimanche newspaper and BFM radio and made public on Saturday.</p>
<p>			   percentage  projected seats in</p>
<p>			    of vote    National Assembly</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		2.5	    0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		 10	    20-28</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left  27	   190-220</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists		  6.5	    0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR/UDF-other right    39.5	 305-345</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front	   14	     0-3</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Other			 0.5	    0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p>A previous IFOP poll dated May 9 gave the Communists 16-20 seats, Socialists and other left 177-207 seats, the RPR/UDF and other right 328-358 seats and the National Front 0-3 seats.</p>
</text>
